cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use canli-validation-mcp, please cite the software and its author."
title: "canli-validation-mcp: an MCP server that validates backtests"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Canli"
    given-names: "Arhan"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-4138-7907"
repository-code: "https://github.com/arhancanli/canli-validation-mcp"
url: "https://canlicapital.com/developers"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - model context protocol
  - backtest overfitting
  - deflated Sharpe ratio
  - quantitative finance
abstract: >-
  A Model Context Protocol server that validates a trading backtest for an AI coding assistant:
  deflated Sharpe ratio, CSCV probability of backtest overfitting, minimum track record and backtest
  length, haircut Sharpe ratio and luck-equivalent trials, each checked against its source paper,
  with Ed25519-signed receipts and a statement of what each result does not establish.
